   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`delete INDEX` now works, and `python tools/check.py` passes: all 6 tests pass and there are no line-length violations.\n\n**Red:** I wrote the tests first and ran the checks, which failed 4 of the 6 tests. The two store tests errored with `AttributeError: module 'fieldnotes.store' has no attribute 'delete'`. The two CLI tests failed with exit code 2, because `delete` was an unknown command.\n\n**Green:**\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py`:** `delete(index)` removes and returns the note at that position. It raises `IndexError` for an out-of-range index, including negative ones, and leaves the file unchanged in that case.\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py`:** `delete INDEX` prints `deleted: <text>` and exits 0. An out-of-range index prints `no note at index N` to stderr and exits 1. A missing or non-numeric index prints the usage line and exits 2. I moved the usage text into one `USAGE` constant that now mentions `delete`.\n- **Tests:** I added two tests to `tests/test_store.py` and a new `tests/test_cli.py` with three.\n\n- **0-based index:** `INDEX` is 0-based because `list` doesn't print numbers. If you'd rather have 1-based, or have `list` show each note's index, tell me and I'll change it.\n- **`NOTES_HOME` for the check script:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set. I pointed it at a throwaway temp directory, so your real notes weren't touched.",
